--TEST--
With no controlling terminal the width and height are exactly the documented `80` by `24`, and the colour depth beside them is `None` — `rule:tooling/the-terminal-profile-resolves-once`'s fallback, both dimensions named together
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 3's table: "the controlling terminal's columns/rows, `80`/`24` when there
// is none". A conformance case's streams are all captured, so this run is the
// "when there is none" half, and the pair is frozen here because a member that
// answered `0`, or that answered a width and forgot the height, prints
// plausibly against either line alone.
//
// `80` is not arbitrary: it is the width every terminal has had since the
// punched card, and a program that subtracts a margin from `width` must be
// able to do it without checking for zero first.

if (Core\Cli::isTty(Core\Cli\Stream::Out)) {
    echo "a terminal is attached", "\n";
} else {
    echo "no terminal", "\n";
}

uint $columns = Core\Cli::width();
uint $rows = Core\Cli::height();
echo "width=", $columns, "\n";
echo "height=", $rows, "\n";

if (Core\Cli::colorDepth() == Core\Cli\ColorDepth::None) {
    echo "depth=None", "\n";
} else {
    echo "depth=some", "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
no terminal
width=80
height=24
depth=None
